  "correction_rules": [
    "Reduce forecast overshoots following sharp price spikes, especially when sentiment is neutral or negative.",
    "Adjust downward for persistent overestimation in early 30-day forecasts when sentiment is consistently low or negative.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias correction when forecasted prices deviate >15% from recent 5-day average, especially after high sentiment volatility.",
    "Lower forecasted prices when sentiment history includes multiple negative entries (e.g., >2 consecutive negative sentiment values).",
    "Increase downward bias in forecasts when true outcomes show strong downward momentum (e.g., 3+ consecutive declines) and sentiment is neutral or negative.",
    "Avoid overreacting to short-term sentiment shifts; delay correction until 2–3 days after sentiment change to avoid noise amplification."
  ]
